  "notes": "A する verb composed of {潜|せん} (dive, submerge) + {水|すい} (water). Used for both human diving and submarine operations.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {潜水|せんすい}{艦|かん}: submarine\n- {潜水|せんすい}{士|し}: professional diver\n- {潜水|せんすい}{服|ふく}: diving suit\n- {潜水|せんすい}{病|びょう}: decompression sickness (the bends)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {潜|もぐ}る: to dive, to go under water — everyday native Japanese word for the same action\n- ダイビング: diving (loanword) — usually refers to recreational scuba diving\n- {素潜|すもぐ}り: free diving, skin diving — diving without equipment",
